WEBVTT

00:03.500 --> 00:04.300
Dear mother,

00:05.110 --> 00:08.690
Why do I have to be called a thief and run from the police?

00:10.240 --> 00:14.090
I fixed the dress that Rosemary tore up.

00:15.000 --> 00:16.660
But this is too much!

00:26.630 --> 00:27.790
NAAJA

00:26.630 --> 00:27.790
Nadja

00:27.820 --> 00:30.290
kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:27.840 --> 00:30.290
With your eyes

00:30.290 --> 00:31.450
NAAJA

00:30.340 --> 00:31.450
Nadja

00:31.470 --> 00:33.720
nani ga mieru

00:31.470 --> 00:33.720
What do you see?

00:33.940 --> 00:36.830
haruka tooku hikaru

00:33.940 --> 00:36.830
Shining in the far distance,

00:36.980 --> 00:39.120
mirai no tobira

00:36.980 --> 00:39.120
The door to the future,

00:40.260 --> 00:43.670
sagashiteiru

00:40.260 --> 00:43.670
That's what I'm searching for

00:43.670 --> 00:50.880
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.590 --> 00:55.000
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:55.100 --> 00:58.360
arasoimo kitto nakunaru

00:55.100 --> 00:58.360
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:58.430 --> 01:01.810
kon nani mo tanoshiku naru

00:58.460 --> 01:01.810
It could be so much more fun

01:01.840 --> 01:05.290
sekai wa hiruikedo hitotsune

01:01.840 --> 01:05.290
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:05.660 --> 01:09.020
tabi no owari wa mienai

01:05.660 --> 01:09.020
I can't see the end of the journey

01:09.050 --> 01:12.210
kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:09.050 --> 01:12.210
God is the only one who can possibly know

01:12.380 --> 01:16.030
itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:12.380 --> 01:16.030
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:16.030 --> 01:18.180
te wo furinagara

01:16.030 --> 01:18.180
I will go waving

01:18.330 --> 01:25.070
toki ni wa BURUU ni naru himo aru kedo

01:18.330 --> 01:25.070
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:25.070 --> 01:27.810
ushiro mukanai

01:25.070 --> 01:27.810
But I won't look back

01:28.080 --> 01:33.120
yume ga kanau hima de

01:28.080 --> 01:33.120
Until the day my dream comes true

01:33.290 --> 01:36.670
NAAJA kimi no hoho emi wa

01:33.290 --> 01:36.670
Nadja, your smile

01:36.750 --> 01:39.950
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:36.750 --> 01:39.950
Nadja, you give me courage

01:40.250 --> 01:43.210
aoi sora no shita de

01:40.250 --> 01:43.210
Under the blue sky

01:43.190 --> 01:46.000
ashita no yukue

01:43.190 --> 01:46.000
I will find the place

01:46.520 --> 01:50.150
mitsu kerukara

01:46.520 --> 01:50.150
Where my future lies

02:04.160 --> 02:05.270
Dear Ms. Director,

02:06.090 --> 02:09.390
Due to some circumstances, I have returned to Paris.

02:10.850 --> 02:15.370
There is something I need advice about, so I may be returning to Applefield soon.

02:16.700 --> 02:18.680
I hope you will be able to help me.

02:19.590 --> 02:23.690
While I'm in Paris, I think I will try to go see Oliver.

02:28.430 --> 02:29.560
Rosemary...

02:30.330 --> 02:33.420
What is she trying to accomplish by impersonating me?

02:40.560 --> 02:44.480
Morning of Decision! The Journey of Truth

02:48.940 --> 02:49.990
Here, catch!

02:52.060 --> 02:52.900
Here!

02:56.580 --> 02:58.380
I wonder what we should do from here on out...

02:58.880 --> 03:00.500
Even if you ask that...

03:01.340 --> 03:06.230
We've come back to Paris after running from the police in Vienna. That's fine, but...

03:06.820 --> 03:11.050
Under these circumstances, she would stand out in places like a public park.

03:11.320 --> 03:12.550
What are you trying to say?

03:13.070 --> 03:14.010
Well...

03:14.550 --> 03:18.180
We may as well go to Kennosuke's country, Japan.

03:18.300 --> 03:21.340
Then even the police couldn't come after her.

03:22.010 --> 03:23.510
What do we do about money?

03:25.760 --> 03:28.110
We are traveling performers.

03:28.500 --> 03:32.300
If we have no place to perform, we can't earn any money.

03:32.520 --> 03:34.870
That's the same as not being able to go anywhere.

03:34.920 --> 03:37.140
Like I said, what are you trying to say?

03:37.410 --> 03:39.860
It's not about "what I want to say," it's more about what I want to hear.

03:40.330 --> 03:42.130
What are we supposed to do?

03:42.230 --> 03:43.730
This isn't the time to lose our cool.

03:45.140 --> 03:46.030
Granny...

03:47.110 --> 03:49.440
For the time being, let's sell hats.

03:49.560 --> 03:51.510
The rest will fall together somehow.

03:52.180 --> 03:54.570
Nothing will come from that!

03:54.720 --> 03:55.900
For Nadja, too!

03:55.900 --> 03:59.850
If she keeps running with us, she won't meet her mother.

04:00.030 --> 04:00.920
Thomas!

04:02.500 --> 04:04.220
It will work out somehow.

04:04.470 --> 04:06.770
We've made it this far.

04:06.960 --> 04:08.370
But...

04:08.440 --> 04:09.480
We're fine

04:10.070 --> 04:15.040
But in Nadja's case, she can't give up, no matter what the reason.

04:16.150 --> 04:17.040
That's right...

04:19.650 --> 04:22.470
It's been a while since we were in Paris.

04:22.840 --> 04:24.470
Brings back memories!

04:24.810 --> 04:29.550
This is where we met TJ and it's the first place where we searched for your mother, right?

04:30.540 --> 04:32.610
I wonder how Madeline is doing?

04:32.890 --> 04:36.220
That painter, too...I wonder if he's still making portraits?

04:37.480 --> 04:38.510
Hey, Nadja!

04:38.610 --> 04:40.510
At least pay attention to me!

04:41.620 --> 04:44.040
I have to hurry and find Oliver.

04:45.280 --> 04:46.610
Oliver?

04:46.760 --> 04:49.350
He's your friend from Applefield, right?

04:49.480 --> 04:50.120
Yes.

04:50.780 --> 04:52.680
Because he knows Rosemary

04:53.080 --> 04:59.180
I'm going to ask him to help me prove that I'm the real Nadja and that I've worn this brooch since I was small.

05:00.580 --> 05:01.300
Oh, I see.

05:01.600 --> 05:03.940
Then there will be no objections.

05:04.610 --> 05:08.680
Even so, we've tried to convince them before without success.

05:08.980 --> 05:11.420
It's true that it's been difficult...

05:12.610 --> 05:13.470
Hello!

05:13.770 --> 05:15.250
Oh, you are...

05:15.770 --> 05:17.590
Oliver's girlfriend, right?

05:18.430 --> 05:19.590
No, you're wrong!

05:19.840 --> 05:21.370
Oh, I'm wrong?

05:21.450 --> 05:22.430
That's too bad.

05:22.900 --> 05:25.470
Anyway, I came to see Oliver.

05:26.010 --> 05:26.830
Oliver?

05:27.100 --> 05:29.250
There's something important I need to ask him.

05:31.120 --> 05:32.090
I'm sorry...

05:32.560 --> 05:34.310
But Oliver doesn't work here anymore.

05:34.530 --> 05:36.600
What? Did he quit?

05:37.150 --> 05:38.630
No, that's not it.

05:38.680 --> 05:39.790
So, where is he?

05:41.390 --> 05:42.780
Hm, let's see...

05:42.900 --> 05:45.610
He should be in Russia by now!

05:45.910 --> 05:46.950
Russia?

05:47.490 --> 05:51.420
If you remember him, Oliver had pretty strong arms, didn't he?

05:51.840 --> 05:56.400
The boss knew he was going places.

05:56.870 --> 05:57.710
If that's the case...

05:58.030 --> 06:03.090
He accompanied the boss to assist him.

06:03.370 --> 06:07.510
It's a shame, but he won't be back for a while.

06:10.330 --> 06:13.040
Well, let's not give up. Cheer up!

06:14.840 --> 06:15.980
I'm fine.

06:17.310 --> 06:21.120
That's because I've learned that Oliver is fulfilling his dream.

06:21.580 --> 06:23.460
So, I also have to do my best.

06:24.970 --> 06:25.710
I see.

06:25.980 --> 06:27.290
Well, then it's alright.

06:28.000 --> 06:29.290
But, we still haven't met him.

06:32.400 --> 06:33.340
Well, let's go back.

06:43.930 --> 06:45.410
What's going on?

06:51.460 --> 06:52.270
Hey, they're...

06:52.320 --> 06:53.800
Nadja, hide!

06:57.130 --> 06:57.850
What's wrong?

06:58.120 --> 06:58.810
Be quiet.

06:59.700 --> 07:00.620
It's the Vienna police.

07:01.970 --> 07:04.290
Enough. Just hand her over.

07:04.760 --> 07:08.390
Even if you say that...

07:09.600 --> 07:13.770
Hand over the thief that you're hiding in your troupe.

07:13.950 --> 07:15.770
Will you cooperate with us?

07:16.490 --> 07:17.770
Sorry, Mr. Policeman.

07:18.320 --> 07:21.850
But even if you say this girl is here, we don't have anyone here like that.

07:22.170 --> 07:24.320
Do you intend to have us search through everything?

07:24.410 --> 07:26.320
Even if you do that.

07:26.320 --> 07:28.320
I will state this clearly.

07:28.590 --> 07:29.920
Bring out the dancing girl.

07:31.990 --> 07:36.590
There should be a dancing girl with blue eyes and platinum blonde hair whose name is Nadja.

07:36.860 --> 07:38.410
You will bring that girl out.

07:39.030 --> 07:40.020
This Nadja...

07:40.540 --> 07:42.760
Now, who could that be?

07:43.870 --> 07:45.050
Are you Nadja?

07:46.360 --> 07:46.980
How about you?

07:48.460 --> 07:49.600
And how about you?

07:51.470 --> 07:53.820
I'm also not Nadja, by the way.

07:54.110 --> 07:55.770
That's obvious just by looking!

07:56.040 --> 07:58.090
Then, can you please leave?

07:58.360 --> 08:00.010
Nobody here is called Nadja...

07:59.670 --> 08:01.120
Then, how do you explain this?

08:02.700 --> 08:03.120
Oh!

08:03.320 --> 08:04.480
That is...

08:04.880 --> 08:08.560
This is a poster of your performance in Salsburg.

08:08.630 --> 08:10.160
The evidence is accumulating.

08:10.280 --> 08:12.780
Well, I wonder what that is...

08:13.490 --> 08:15.150
You're still playing dumb?

08:15.250 --> 08:17.590
Nadja is written right here, isn't it?

08:17.710 --> 08:18.830
Right here!

08:20.260 --> 08:24.400
Look closer. It's written <i>Nanja,</i> not Nadja.

08:24.580 --> 08:26.530
You read it wrong, you idiot!

08:27.790 --> 08:31.370
Then bring out Nanja, Kanja, or whoever out!

08:32.550 --> 08:33.370
I don't understand you...

08:33.370 --> 08:34.920
This thing...!

08:39.560 --> 08:41.070
How could you do that?

08:43.410 --> 08:45.220
Now you don't have any evidence.

08:46.380 --> 08:47.710
Messing around with me...

08:47.930 --> 08:52.800
If you continue to be uncooperative, I have ways to deal with you.

08:53.040 --> 08:53.910
You have ways?

08:54.400 --> 08:56.200
Well, well then!

08:57.140 --> 08:58.000
G-get him!

08:58.080 --> 08:59.260
Arrest this man!

09:03.290 --> 09:04.690
Let's help the chief!

09:07.290 --> 09:10.620
Take this!

09:11.310 --> 09:14.100
And this, and that!

09:15.900 --> 09:17.040
This is my fault...

09:22.320 --> 09:24.570
George, calm down a little.

09:24.740 --> 09:27.530
What do you hope to accomplish by rebelling against the authorities?

09:28.810 --> 09:30.590
That goes for you too, Mr. Policeman.

09:31.550 --> 09:35.920
Do you really have time to be messing around here?

09:37.130 --> 09:39.330
Calm down a bit first, okay?

09:39.680 --> 09:41.330
Then we can talk.

09:42.570 --> 09:43.330
I understand.

09:43.630 --> 09:46.050
However, this big one is coming with us.

09:46.420 --> 09:49.280
He has to take responsibility.

09:49.480 --> 09:49.920
Yeah.

09:58.960 --> 10:00.740
Kennosuke! Let go of me!

10:00.860 --> 10:01.350
No.

10:02.560 --> 10:05.720
If they take me, they won't take the chief.

10:06.190 --> 10:08.560
Do you want to make his sacrifice for nothing?

10:09.250 --> 10:12.390
He purposely let himself be taken so he could protect you.

10:15.600 --> 10:17.370
Then...because of me...

10:17.600 --> 10:18.510
That's not it!

10:20.560 --> 10:22.020
It's not your fault.

10:22.580 --> 10:24.680
Everyone understands that.

10:26.210 --> 10:27.180
Kennosuke...

10:27.940 --> 10:30.090
It's okay, leave everything to me.

10:32.480 --> 10:37.270
Anyway, first we have to get back to the car to join up with everybody.

11:09.890 --> 11:10.430
Understand?

11:10.950 --> 11:13.960
Wait right here until I call for you.

11:13.960 --> 11:14.600
Okay.

11:18.470 --> 11:19.930
Hey hey, you two!

11:20.350 --> 11:21.660
I appreciate your efforts!

11:23.730 --> 11:24.350
Everyone!

11:27.090 --> 11:27.880
Nadja is...

11:28.300 --> 11:30.350
Yes, she's hiding nearby.

11:30.860 --> 11:34.150
But she can't get here with the police in the way.

11:34.220 --> 11:37.730
Kennosuke, how many are out there?

11:37.950 --> 11:38.470
Two.

11:40.070 --> 11:42.590
Let's create a diversion.

11:42.840 --> 11:44.150
Alright, let's split up.

11:45.410 --> 11:46.810
Leave it to me.

11:47.970 --> 11:49.430
I have an idea.

11:56.100 --> 11:57.900
Then, according to the plan...

12:08.960 --> 12:11.800
Cream, Chocolat, what's wrong?

12:12.340 --> 12:12.730
Huh?

12:13.200 --> 12:15.130
You're getting Nadja's scent?

12:20.710 --> 12:22.630
Ah, wait for me!

12:22.960 --> 12:23.820
Cream!

12:23.820 --> 12:24.980
Chocolat!

12:33.180 --> 12:33.790
Nadja

12:34.190 --> 12:34.850
Hurry.

12:36.140 --> 12:37.320
Hurry!

12:38.340 --> 12:41.960
Wait, Cream, Chocolat!

12:52.900 --> 12:53.810
They've separated!

12:54.140 --> 12:55.390
You follow that one!

12:55.370 --> 12:56.060
Right!

13:13.490 --> 13:14.580
Oh, it's there?

13:26.620 --> 13:28.250
Bad luck, huh?

13:56.300 --> 13:57.800
It was a big success!

14:04.150 --> 14:07.380
I wish I could have seen the stupid looks painted on the policemen's faces!

14:08.370 --> 14:09.930
Rita, Cream, Chocolat

14:10.170 --> 14:10.960
You were the stars!

14:12.840 --> 14:15.090
Should I become an actress?

14:15.210 --> 14:16.300
That would be great.

14:16.670 --> 14:19.360
But you should practice your verbal expression a bit more first.

14:19.700 --> 14:21.210
Hey

14:24.710 --> 14:28.420
Well then, what should we do when the chief gets back?

14:29.110 --> 14:29.550
Um...

14:30.120 --> 14:31.260
About that...

14:35.280 --> 14:37.820
I've thought about it a lot...

14:39.010 --> 14:42.560
Just like I thought, I can't cause you any more trouble.

14:42.860 --> 14:44.020
What's this about?

14:46.490 --> 14:48.640
Isn't that too cold?

14:49.030 --> 14:51.350
You're not being troublesome to us.

14:52.140 --> 14:53.030
Kennosuke...

14:53.330 --> 14:55.800
If you leave us, what will you do?

14:56.290 --> 15:00.460
In times like these, shouldn't we be cooperating with each other?

15:01.150 --> 15:02.830
Aren't we friends?

15:03.300 --> 15:06.020
That's easy to think when you're not the victim.

15:06.460 --> 15:06.810
Huh?

15:07.520 --> 15:09.470
Think of it from Nadja's perspective.

15:10.780 --> 15:17.050
To continue traveling with us would be painful with everything that's going on.

15:18.010 --> 15:21.150
Even if we keep running, we won't really get anywhere.

15:21.320 --> 15:23.990
So then what do we do, Thomas?

15:24.090 --> 15:25.590
Stop it, Kennosuke.

15:28.880 --> 15:29.670
Sorry.

15:31.470 --> 15:32.060
Nadja

15:32.950 --> 15:34.360
I'm sure you already know this

15:34.750 --> 15:38.110
But everyone's just trying to look out for you when they say such things.

15:38.650 --> 15:39.220
I know.

15:44.500 --> 15:46.730
No matter what tricks we use

15:47.420 --> 15:49.660
The police will come after us wherever we go.

15:50.480 --> 15:53.930
While I'm here, no one can even sleep peacefully.

15:55.220 --> 15:58.230
And because we can't perform anymore, we can't earn any money.

15:59.610 --> 16:00.500
That's the limit.

16:01.910 --> 16:04.720
I can't be a burden to everyone anymore.

16:08.720 --> 16:09.690
That's why I...

16:10.300 --> 16:11.410
Wait a minute!

16:14.570 --> 16:15.240
Chief!

16:15.980 --> 16:16.620
Why...

16:16.990 --> 16:17.460
What?

16:18.050 --> 16:21.040
Granny's aristocrat friend lent me a hand.

16:22.700 --> 16:24.670
Anyway, that doesn't matter.

16:27.980 --> 16:28.520
Nadja

16:30.450 --> 16:31.810
What do you want to do?

16:32.130 --> 16:32.550
Huh?

16:33.460 --> 16:37.160
If you want to stay here, then you can stay here forever.

16:40.590 --> 16:45.240
Saying things like "I'm causing trouble" or "If only I weren't here" doesn't really matter.

16:47.950 --> 16:48.670
I...

16:50.250 --> 16:54.050
Whatever may come, whatever may happen, we will protect you without hesitation.

16:54.810 --> 16:56.860
Don't think about trivial things.

17:01.850 --> 17:02.520
Nadja

17:02.860 --> 17:04.790
What would you like to do?

17:10.420 --> 17:11.280
Mother...

17:17.500 --> 17:18.090
Chief

17:18.540 --> 17:19.080
Everyone

17:20.240 --> 17:21.330
Thank you.

17:23.060 --> 17:24.830
I want to stay with you.

17:25.620 --> 17:26.690
I want to stay here forever with everyone.

17:27.750 --> 17:28.170
But...

17:30.910 --> 17:33.520
I really do want to meet my mother afterall.

17:34.240 --> 17:35.820
That's why I'll go alone.

17:37.600 --> 17:38.190
Everyone

17:39.100 --> 17:40.390
Thank you for worrying about me.

17:41.600 --> 17:42.530
That's fine then.

18:10.090 --> 18:10.800
Kennosuke

18:12.780 --> 18:13.470
Nadja

18:13.790 --> 18:15.250
It's not much, but...

18:16.010 --> 18:16.600
You can't!

18:17.050 --> 18:20.410
That's the money you saved so you can see your little sister, right?

18:21.760 --> 18:24.160
It's fine. At least with this much...

18:24.700 --> 18:26.230
I will just accept your good intentions.

18:27.420 --> 18:31.470
Granny and Abel already gave me some money.

18:32.160 --> 18:33.170
So don't worry.

18:34.480 --> 18:35.020
Nadja

18:35.860 --> 18:36.430
I...

18:37.590 --> 18:41.410
I got instructions from Thomas about how to travel alone.

18:42.670 --> 18:45.360
From Sylvie, I received a purse set.

18:45.960 --> 18:48.180
Rita gave me candy to cheer me up.

18:49.120 --> 18:52.720
And Cream and Chocolat gave me their favorite bones.

18:54.670 --> 18:55.560
What about the chief?

18:55.860 --> 18:56.300
Huh?

18:56.670 --> 18:59.260
Didn't the chief give you anything?

19:01.090 --> 19:03.560
The chief gave me courage.

19:05.310 --> 19:09.290
So please...keep a smile on your face too.

19:24.320 --> 19:25.530
Be careful.

19:26.100 --> 19:28.000
Don't get tricked again.

19:32.720 --> 19:33.830
Nadja!

19:41.360 --> 19:43.920
Keep practicing your dancing.

19:44.390 --> 19:45.920
Well, you'll be fine.

19:49.450 --> 19:50.740
Hey, Kennosuke.

20:33.170 --> 20:35.790
Everyone, thank you for everything.

20:36.900 --> 20:38.560
I can't even tell you how grateful I am.

20:39.740 --> 20:43.030
I may be leaving, but I won't say goodbye.

20:44.410 --> 20:46.230
I believe we will see each other again.

20:47.810 --> 20:48.330
That's why...

20:49.390 --> 20:49.890
That's why...

20:52.780 --> 20:55.470
Like I thought, Nadja is great.

20:56.580 --> 20:57.470
Of course.

20:57.990 --> 21:02.210
Nadja is Dandelion's miraculous dancing princess, after all.

21:17.140 --> 21:19.140
Well...I'll be going now.

21:30.970 --> 21:31.590
Mother...

21:32.300 --> 21:33.070
Wait for me!

21:40.920 --> 21:44.840
Nadja took one step closer to a new destiny.

21:45.760 --> 21:48.990
Sometimes we just have to go against the wind.

22:14.540 --> 22:17.800
RONDON donyori haretara PARI

22:14.540 --> 22:17.800
Paris is sunnier than London

22:17.970 --> 22:20.990
KARUMEN menyori PAERIYA suki

22:17.970 --> 22:20.990
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:21.430 --> 22:27.630
SUPEEDO no jyoou kimagure yasan

22:21.430 --> 22:27.630
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:28.540 --> 22:29.800
kitto

22:28.540 --> 22:29.800
Indeed

22:32.560 --> 22:35.030
nayan datte muda yo

22:32.560 --> 22:35.030
It's no use worrying about it

22:35.080 --> 22:38.690
kesera sera sera sera

22:35.080 --> 22:38.690
Que sera sera, sera sera

22:38.930 --> 22:43.620
ashita nante itsumo naru youni

22:38.930 --> 22:43.620
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:43.720 --> 22:45.080
naru naru

22:43.720 --> 22:45.080
